The '''Marbassa Arsenal''' ({{lang-bl|Arsenal de Marbassa}}), also known as '''Marbassa Naval Base''' is a group of ports and land facilities of the [[Confederal Navy]] (''Marina confederales''), which are scattered in multiple districts of [[Marbassa]], [[Dríadas]] region. Since the [[Camboriú War]], it has undergone continuous strengthening as the main base of the Confederal Navy on the [[Sea of Shuainia]] side of [[Cerdanya]], with a vast defensive range from the  Sea of Shuainia and the [[Salsipuedes Sea]], to the far-flung islands of [[Cap de Pingüins]] (including the [[Boreal Islands]]). 

Today, Marbassa is the home base for one-fourth of the Confederal Navy surface fleet, including one [[w:helicopter carrier|helicopter carrier]], ''[[BB Talcahuano (DDH-84)|Talcahuano]]''. Naval logistics, accommodation and messing are provided on site, with personnel support functions (e.g. medical and dental; education; pastoral and welfare) provided by [[Naval Equipment and Support]], alongside other functions and departments, e.g. Navy Command Headquarters support staff. The base is additionally home to a number of military shore activities, including the ship repair and maintenance facility operated by [[Astilleros Baliscanos]].

